│                                                                    │
│  2 What is the relationship between this part of the code and the  │
│    bug?                                                            │
│                                                                    │
│  • The bug is about premature loop exit when the LLM returns only  │
│    thinking blocks (without text or tool_use).                     │
│  • The loop currently exits when it gets a Msg from _reasoning,    │
│    assuming it contains usable output.                             │
│  • However, _reasoning can produce Msgs that only have thinking    │
│    content blocks, which should not cause exit because no          │
│    user-visible text was produced.                                 │
│  • So, the logic for exiting on receiving a Msg should be modified │
│    to check if that Msg contains actual text content before        │
│    breaking the loop and returning it.                             │
│  • Otherwise, the loop should continue when no text blocks exist,  │
│    to allow further reasoning iterations to generate useful        │
│    output.                                                         │
│                                                                    │
│  3 Given the issue description, what would be the intended         │
│    behavior of this part of the code?                              │
│                                                                    │
